@startuml
title Multi-Machine Predictive Maintenance UML/Class Diagram

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontColor #1F2937
skinparam classBorderColor #374151
skinparam classBackgroundColor #F9FAFB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
skinparam arrowColor #374151

note as Purpose
  Purpose:
  Shows the main software/domain classes and relationships for
  a factory with multiple monitored machines. It documents why
  the design uses one ESP32 sensor node per machine and how
  telemetry and alerts move through MQTT, gateway, cloud, and dashboard.
end note

class Factory {
  +factoryId: String
  +name: String
  +location: String
}

class Machine {
  +machineId: String
  +name: String
  +type: MachineType
  +healthState: HealthState
}

class SensorModule {
  +moduleId: String
  +machineId: String
  +samplingRate: Hz
  +publishTelemetry()
  +receiveAlert()
}

class ESP32SensorNode {
  +nodeId: String
  +wifiMac: String
  +firmwareVersion: String
  +readSensors()
  +tagRecord()
  +bufferIfOffline()
}

class "Temperature\nSensor" as TemperatureSensor {
  +sensorId: String
  +valueC: Float
  +interface: 1-Wire/SPI/ADC
  +readTemperature()
}

class "Vibration\nSensor" as VibrationSensor {
  +sensorId: String
  +acceleration: Float
  +interface: I2C/SPI/ADC
  +readVibration()
}

class TelemetryRecord {
  +recordId: String
  +timestamp: DateTime
  +machineId: String
  +temperature: Float
  +vibrationRms: Float
  +riskScore: Float
}

class "Gateway" as Gateway {
  +gatewayId: String
  +networkType: String
  +forwardTelemetry()
  +routeAlert()
}

class "MQTT\nBroker" as MQTTBroker {
  +brokerUrl: String
  +telemetryTopic: String
  +alertTopic: String
}

class "Cloud\nPlatform" as CloudPlatform {
  +ingestTelemetry()
  +storeHistory()
  +analyzeMachineHealth()
}

class "Alert\nService" as AlertService {
  +evaluateSeverity()
  +generateAlert()
  +publishEdgeCommand()
}

class "Dashboard" as Dashboard {
  +showMachineStatus()
  +showTrends()
  +acknowledgeAlert()
}

enum MachineType {
  Motor
  Pump
  Fan
  Compressor
  Conveyor
}

enum HealthState {
  Healthy
  Degrading
  Faulty
  Critical
}

Factory "1" o-- "1..*" Machine : contains
Machine "1" *-- "1" SensorModule : monitored by
SensorModule "1" *-- "1" ESP32SensorNode : controller
SensorModule "1" *-- "1" TemperatureSensor : local wired sensor
SensorModule "1" *-- "1" VibrationSensor : local wired sensor
SensorModule "1" --> "0..*" TelemetryRecord : creates

ESP32SensorNode --> Gateway : MQTT over Wi-Fi\ntelemetry publish
Gateway --> MQTTBroker : forwards messages
MQTTBroker --> CloudPlatform : telemetry topic
CloudPlatform --> AlertService : abnormal state
AlertService --> MQTTBroker : alert/command topic
MQTTBroker --> Gateway : alert route
Gateway --> ESP32SensorNode : edge alert\nfull-duplex path
CloudPlatform --> Dashboard : status, trends, KPIs
Dashboard --> AlertService : acknowledgement

note right of SensorModule
  Recommended design:
  one ESP32 sensor node per machine.

  Sensors are wired locally to the ESP32,
  while machine data is sent upstream using
  MQTT over Wi-Fi.
end note

note bottom of Gateway
  Industrial scalability option:
  RS485/Modbus can replace or complement
  Wi-Fi where wired, noise-resistant field
  communication is required.
end note

legend bottom
|= UML Symbol / Arrow |= Meaning in this diagram |
| 1, 1..*, 0..* | Multiplicity: exactly one, one or more, zero or more |
| o-- | Aggregation: factory contains machines as assets |
| *-- | Composition: machine owns its monitoring module; module owns its local parts |
| --> | Communication, creation, or data/control dependency |
| MQTT over Wi-Fi | Primary telemetry path from ESP32 node to gateway/cloud |
| edge alert path | Return path for alert/command messages back to ESP32 |
endlegend
@enduml
